@meta
id: 07-10
title: Drill — one sentence per line
chapter: 07
type: drill
skills: paragraph-motion
par: 50
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: click before each second sentence, Enter, Backspace over the space
open: policy.md

@brief
The team has moved its docs to one sentence per line so that review diffs
stay readable. Eight lines, two sentences each. Split every line at the
sentence boundary.

Nothing to work out. The trailing space left behind does not matter; the
grader ignores it, as does git. Neither does the last `)` of the last rep,
which has nowhere to go.

@keys
| `)` | forward to the start of the next sentence |
| `i` `Enter` | break the line in front of the cursor |

@hints
The rep is five keys: `)` to land on the second sentence, `i` `Enter` `Esc`
to push it onto a line of its own, then `)` again to step onto the next
line.
--
That closing `)` is what makes every rep identical. It leaves you at the
start of a line, so the `)` that opens the next rep lands mid-line, where a
break is actually wanted. Eight identical reps, no `j` between them.

@solution
    ) i <Enter> <Esc> )   eight times, then :wq<Enter>

Forty-three keystrokes to reflow eight lines.

Reformatting prose is the job that turns people back into mouse users,
because it looks like it needs precision: find the boundary, click exactly
between the full stop and the capital, do not eat the space. `)` removes all
of that. It knows where the sentence starts, so the only thing left for you
to decide is what to do when you get there.

Note what you did not do: you never pressed `j`, never looked at a line
number, and never checked where you were. The rep carried you down the file
on its own. That is the sign of a well-chosen motion.

The one thing to watch is that `i` `Enter` at the very start of a line
leaves an empty line rather than splitting anything, which is why the rep
is built to land you mid-line every time.

@start policy.md
A refund is always issued against an order. The customer record is never touched.
Amounts are in minor units. A refund may not exceed the order total.
Partial refunds are allowed. They may be repeated until the total is reached.
The window is thirty days. Outside it the cancellation still succeeds.
Every provider call carries an idempotency key. The key comes from the refund id.
A failed refund is retried by the nightly job. The caller never retries in the request path.
Receipts are queued rather than sent inline. A mail failure cannot fail the refund.
Webhook signatures are checked before parsing. Replays are answered with a 200 and ignored.

@expected policy.md
